+        // SPIKE-LOCAL PATCH (not upstream): `.copy`, where upstream has `.process`.
+        //
+        // Upstream compiles the Metal GPU renderer's shader at BUILD time. That cannot
+        // work here: Xcode 26.6 moved the Metal toolchain to a downloadable component
+        // (`xcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain`) which is not installed, and
+        // this machine has Command Line Tools only. Measured, not assumed —
+        // `.process("Shaders.metal")` fails with:
+        //
+        //     error: unable to spawn process 'metal' (No such file or directory)
+        //     error: CompileMetalFile ... failed with a nonzero exit code
+        //
+        // `.copy` skips the Metal compiler entirely and ships the raw .metal SOURCE into
+        // `SwiftTerm_SwiftTerm.bundle/Contents/Resources/`. That is enough, because
+        // MetalTerminalRenderer.makeLibrary (Apple/Metal/MetalTerminalRenderer.swift:2746)
+        // has a third fallback: no default library and no .metallib, then compile the
+        // source at RUNTIME via `device.makeLibrary(source:)` (:2765), which goes through
+        // the OS Metal compiler service and needs no offline toolchain. Measured on an
+        // M4 Pro: 173ms on the first call, ~0ms after (the OS caches it), all seven
+        // required shader functions present, real MTLRenderPipelineState created.
+        //
+        // THIS PATCH USED TO SAY `exclude:`, AND THAT WAS THE BUG. Excluding the file
+        // removes it from the bundle, so the runtime fallback cannot find it either and
+        // throws `shaderSourceMissing` (:2762) — meaning the GPU renderer was
+        // unreachable, silently, and the app had no way to report why. Avoiding the
+        // build-time compiler required dropping `.process`; it never required dropping
+        // the file. See .afk/research/performance-audit-2026-07-31.md §1.
+        //
+        // app/Scripts/make-app-bundle.sh already copies `*.bundle` into
+        // `Contents/Resources/`, which is exactly one of the two locations
+        // `candidateBundles()` (:2828) probes; `swift run` is covered by the other.
         resources: [
-            .process("Apple/Metal/Shaders.metal")
+            .copy("Apple/Metal/Shaders.metal")
         ]
